From 00559be5c318373dbbf0b8f5ce57d7860712571d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DNS: Encrypted DNS fallback, option 162 by policy, Dreadwatch
 exempt devices, Wallguard lists tab

- Encrypted DNS stage 2: when DNS-over-TLS upstreams stop answering, the router falls back to plain upstream DNS so
  name resolution keeps working, and returns to DNS-over-TLS once it answers again (Strict profile excepted).
- DHCP option 162 (automatic encrypted DNS for devices) is offered only to devices the router's DNS-over-TLS server
  would serve, following DNS Director: a device with an unfiltered or outside-resolver rule is left out, so it no
  longer adopts a resolver that refuses it (iPhones dropping off Wi-Fi).
- Dreadwatch: a list of devices that skip the threat lists, counted per device; the resolver reads it from one file.
- Wallguard: a tab to view and edit the allow and block lists, including names allowed for 24 hours (remove, extend,
  make permanent); entries allowed for 24 hours expire on the regular fold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
